From aeeffe77271723f6a7168df251c1f80e846beaf6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Dr. Hutson" <hutsona@umsystem.edu>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:21:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(pdu): decode Enhanced Security Server Redirection PDU

Share Control pduType 0xA (PDUTYPE_SERVER_REDIR_PKT) previously failed with
"unexpected share control PDU type". Add rdp::server_redirection with
ServerRedirectionPdu (pad2Octets + RDP_SERVER_REDIRECTION_PACKET,
[MS-RDPBCGR] 2.2.13.1 and 2.2.13.3.1), ServerRedirectionFlags and
TargetCertificateContainer, and ShareControlPdu::ServerRedirect.

The header of this PDU carries no shareId. Fields are bounded by the packet
Length, the optional trailing pad is tolerated, the password is kept opaque
and redacted from Debug, and the target certificate (UTF-16LE base64 of
{elementType, encodingType, elementSize, elementData} records) is parsed
without new dependencies. Encoding is supported for server-side use.
